              "type": "text",
              "left": 60,
              "top": 60,
              "width": 880,
              "height": 70,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:32px;\"><strong>Welcome & Course Overview</strong></p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            },
            {
              "id": "text_vTp-UT-q",
              "type": "text",
              "left": 60,
              "top": 160,
              "width": 880,
              "height": 103,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• HTML is the foundation of web pages</p><p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• Course goals: understand document structure, basic elements, and best practices</p><p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• Hands‑on practice building a simple web page</p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            }
          ],
          "background": {
            "type": "solid",
            "color": "#ffffff"
          }
        }
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_ekCCRnsu",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_tjSqlBiN"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_roN0l59f",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Good morning, everyone! I’m Dr. Elena Hart, and today we’ll start our journey into web development by understanding why HTML is the foundation of every web page."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_YWRrlOmB",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_vTp-UT-q"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_Yxb3Kb5g",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "First, HTML provides the basic structure of a page—think of it as the skeleton that holds everything together. Our goal for this lesson is to learn how to create that structure, use common elements like headings, paragraphs, and links, and follow best practices for clean markup."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_jVMZk27n",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_vTp-UT-q"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_5ENp9iPJ",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "By the end of today’s session, each of you will have built a simple web page from scratch, applying what we cover step by step."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_G3Lq40iB",
          "type": "laser",
          "elementId": "text_tjSqlBiN"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_Fp3f0kMf",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Let’s dive in and see how easy it is to turn plain text into a living web page."
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": 1777632718776,
      "updatedAt": 1777632718776
    },
    {
      "id": "scene_hzqYy3Tu4p",
      "stageId": "NDywxqJaL7",
      "type": "slide",
      "title": "Basic HTML Document Structure",
      "order": 2,
      "content": {
        "type": "slide",
        "canvas": {
          "id": "q3hU0zmgdPxRRXoc5sCco",
          "viewportSize": 1000,
          "viewportRatio": 0.5625,
          "theme": {
            "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
            "themeColors": [
              "#5b9bd5",
              "#ed7d31",
              "#a5a5a5",
              "#ffc000",
              "#4472c4"
            ],
            "fontColor": "#333333",
            "fontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
            "outline": {
              "color": "#d14424",
              "width": 2,
              "style": "solid"
            },
            "shadow": {
              "h": 0,
              "v": 0,
              "blur": 10,
              "color": "#000000"
            }
          },
          "elements": [
            {
              "id": "text_mW2AP4AJ",
              "type": "text",
              "left": 60,
              "top": 50,
              "width": 880,
              "height": 70,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:32px;\"><strong>Basic HTML Document Structure</strong></p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            },
            {
              "id": "text_jkKotv0u",
              "type": "text",
              "left": 60,
              "top": 150,
              "width": 880,
              "height": 103,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• <!DOCTYPE html> declares the document type</p><p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• &lt;html&gt;, &lt;head&gt;, &lt;title&gt;, and &lt;body&gt; form the skeleton</p><p style=\"font-size:18px;\">• Minimal HTML page example</p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            },
            {
              "id": "text_fqxYTUIO",
              "type": "text",
              "left": 60,
              "top": 273,
              "width": 880,
              "height": 127,
              "content": "<p style=\"font-size:14px; font-family:monospace;\">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;<br/>&lt;html&gt;<br/>  &lt;head&gt;<br/>    &lt;title&gt;Page Title&lt;/title&gt;<br/>  &lt;/head&gt;<br/>  &lt;body&gt;<br/>    Content goes here.<br/>  &lt;/body&gt;<br/>&lt;/html&gt;</p>",
              "defaultFontName": "Microsoft YaHei",
              "defaultColor": "#333333",
              "rotate": 0
            }
          ],
          "background": {
            "type": "solid",
            "color": "#ffffff"
          }
        }
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "id": "action_c1BT-990",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_mW2AP4AJ"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_Vebvd8ds",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Alright everyone, let's dive into the basic structure that every HTML page needs. This is the foundation for all the web pages you'll build."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_0qkzmZtc",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_jkKotv0u"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_4kou2vc6",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "First, the <code><!DOCTYPE html></code> declaration tells the browser that this is an HTML document. Then we have the main tags: <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>. These form the skeleton of the page."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_HabXjZF7",
          "type": "spotlight",
          "elementId": "text_fqxYTUIO"
        },
        {
          "id": "action_2kpivq1W",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "Here's a minimal example. Notice how the doctype appears at the very top, followed by the opening <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> tag, a <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> section with a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, and finally the <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> where the page content lives. This is all you need to get a valid HTML page running."
        },
        {
          "id": "action_lpfCES_7",
          "type": "speech",
          "text": "To recap, remember: the doctype declaration, the four essential tags, and the simple structure we just saw. With this template, you can start adding your own content inside the body."
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": 1777632754480,
      "updatedAt": 1777632754480
    },
    {
      "id": "scene__ebgg23hfm",
      "stageId": "NDywxqJaL7",
      "type": "interactive",
      "title": "Live HTML Builder",
      "order": 3,
      "content": {
        "type": "interactive",
        "url": "",
        "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <title>Live HTML Builder Playground</title>\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n    <!-- CodeMirror CSS -->\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.13/codemirror.min.css\">\n    <style>\n        body {font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin:0; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; min-height:100vh;}\n        .container {flex:1; display:flex; flex-direction:column; padding:10px;}\n        .editor-output {display:flex; flex:1; gap:10px; min-height:300px;}\n        .editor {flex:1; min-height:300px;}\n        .output {flex:1; border:1px solid #ccc; padding:5px; overflow:auto; background:#fafafa;}\n        .controls {margin-top:10px; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:10px;}\n        button {padding:5px 10px; cursor:pointer;}\n        .hints, .tests {margin-top:10px; border-top:1px solid #ddd; padding-top:10px;}\n        .hint {margin-bottom:5px; display:none;}\n        .test {margin-bottom:5px;}\n        .pass {color:green;}\n        .fail {color:red;}\n        @media (max-width: 600px) {\n            .editor-output {flex-direction:column;}\n        }\n    </style>\n\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.9/dist/katex.min.css\">\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.9/dist/katex.min.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/katex@0.16.9/dist/contrib/auto-render.min.js\"></script>\n<script>\ndocument.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", function() {\n    const katexOptions = {\n        delimiters: [\n            {left: '\\\\[', right: '\\\\]', display: true},\n            {left: '\\\\(', right: '\\\\)', display: false},\n            {left: '$$', right: '$$', display: true},\n            {left: '$', right: '$', display: false}\n        ],\n        throwOnError: false,\n        strict: false,\n        trust: true\n    };\n\n    let renderTimeout;\n    function safeRender() {\n        if (renderTimeout) clearTimeout(renderTimeout);\n        renderTimeout = setTimeout(() => {\n            renderMathInElement(document.body, katexOptions);\n        }, 100);\n    }\n\n    renderMathInElement(document.body, katexOptions);\n\n    const observer = new MutationObserver((mutations) => {\n        let shouldRender = false;\n        mutations.forEach((mutation) => {\n            if (mutation.target &&\n                mutation.target.className &&\n                typeof mutation.target.className === 'string' &&\n                mutation.target.className.includes('katex')) {\n                return;\n            }\n            shouldRender = true;\n        });\n\n        if (shouldRender) {\n            safeRender();\n        }\n    });\n\n    observer.observe(document.body, {\n        childList: true,\n        subtree: true,\n        characterData: true\n    });\n\n    setInterval(() => {\n        const text = document.body.innerText;\n        if (text.includes('\\\\(') || text.includes('$$')) {\n            safeRender();\n        }\n    }, 2000);\n});\n</script>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"container\">\n    <h2>Live HTML Builder</h2>\n    <div class=\"editor-output\">\n        <textarea id=\"code\" class=\"editor\"><!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n    <title>My Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <h1>Welcome</h1>\n    <p>This is a paragraph.</p>\n</body>\n</html></textarea>\n        <div id=\"rendered\" class=\"output\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"controls\">\n        <button id=\"runBtn\">Run</button>\n        <button id=\"hintBtn\">Show Hint</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"hints\">\n        <strong>Hints:</strong>\n        <div class=\"hint\" data-index=\"0\">Try changing the <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> text.</div>\n        <div class=\"hint\" data-index=\"1\">Add another heading like <code>&lt;h2&gt;Subtitle&lt;/h2&gt;</code>.</div>\n        <div class=\"hint\" data-index=\"2\">Modify the paragraph or add a new <code>&lt;p&gt;</code> element.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"tests\">\n        <strong>Test Cases:</strong>\n        <div id=\"testList\"></div>\n    </div>\n    <pre id=\"config\" style=\"display:none;\">{\n  \"type\": \"code\",\n  \"language\": \"html\",\n  \"description\": \"Edit the HTML template and see the result instantly.\",\n  \"starterCode\": \"<!DOCTYPE html>\\\\n<html>\\\\n<head>\\\\n    <title>My Page</title>\\\\n</head>\\\\n<body>\\\\n    <h1>Welcome</h1>\\\\n    <p>This is a paragraph.</p>\\\\n</body>\\\\n</html>\",\n  \"testCases\": [\n    { \"id\": \"t1\", \"description\": \"Contains an h1 element\", \"check\": \"document.querySelector('h1') !== null\" },\n    { \"id\": \"t2\", \"description\": \"Contains a p element\", \"check\": \"document.querySelector('p') !== null\" }\n  ],\n  \"hints\": [\n    \"Try changing the <h1> text.\",\n    \"Add another heading like <h2>Subtitle</h2>.\",\n    \"Modify the paragraph or add a new <p> element.\"\n  ],\n  \"solution\": \"<!DOCTYPE html>\\\\n<html>\\\\n<head>\\\\n    <title>My Page</title>\\\\n</head>\\\\n<body>\\\\n    <h1>Welcome</h1>\\\\n    <p>This is a paragraph.</p>\\\\n</body>\\\\n</html>\"\n}</pre>\n</div>\n\n<!-- CodeMirror JS -->\n<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.13/codemirror.min.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.13/mode/xml/xml.min.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/codemirror/5.65.13/mode/htmlmixed/htmlmixed.min.js\"></script>\n\n<script>\n    // Initialize CodeMirror\n    const editor = CodeMirror.fromTextArea(document.getElementById('code'), {\n        mode: 'htmlmixed',\n        lineNumbers: true,\n        lineWrapping: true,\n        theme: 'default'\n    });\n\n    const runBtn = document.getElementById('runBtn');\n    const hintBtn = document.getElementById('hintBtn');\n    const renderedDiv = document.getElementById('rendered');\n    const hintElements = document.querySelectorAll('.hint');\n    const testList = document.getElementById('testList');\n    const config = JSON.parse(document.getElementById('config').textContent);\n\n    // Run code and render\n    function runCode() {\n        const code = editor.getValue();\n        renderedDiv.innerHTML = code;\n        evaluateTests();\n    }\n\n    runBtn.addEventListener('click', runCode);\n\n    // Show hints progressively\n    let hintIndex = 0;\n    hintBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        if (hintIndex < hintElements.length) {\n            hintElements[hintIndex].style.display = 'block';\n            hintIndex++;\n        } else {\n            alert('No more hints.');\n        }\n    });\n\n    // Build test case UI\n    config.testCases.forEach(test => {\n        const div = document.createElement('div');\n        div.className = 'test';\n        div.id = test.id;\n        div.textContent = test.description + ': ';\n        const span = document.createElement('span');\n        span.textContent = 'Not run';\n        div.appendChild(span);\n        testList.appendChild(div);\n    });\n\n    // Evaluate test cases in the rendered iframe context\n    function evaluateTests() {\n        config.testCases.forEach(test => {\n            let result = false;\n            try {\n                result = eval(test.check);\n            } catch (e) {\n                result = false;\n            }\n            const el = document.getElementById(test.id).querySelector('span');\n            el.textContent = result ? 'Pass' : 'Fail';\n            el.className = result ? 'pass' : 'fail';\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Initial run\n    runCode();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>",
        "widgetType": "code",
        "teacherActions": [
          {
